22. Consideration of the second amendment to the agreement
(231003-30) between Laramie County, WY, and Voss Family Limited
Partnership in the amount of $5,500,000 for the purchase and sale of
real estate at 2020 Carey Ave.
24 - 349
Second Amendment, Voss Family Limited Partnership
Attachments:
Chairman Lovett opened the meeting for PUBLIC COMMENT.  Hearing no PUBLIC
COMMENT, Chairman Lovett closed the comment period.
A motion was made by Commissioner Thompson, seconded by
Commissioner Holmes, that this agenda item be approved.
Commissioner Thompson said he had received a couple of phone calls about the
purchase of the building. He said that both courthouses are full. He noted the county is
obligated to house the judicial system. Commissioner Thompson spoke about the
need for expansion in the future and that building new space at the Archer Complex
would cost 10 times or more than the building in question.
Commissioner Thompson stressed the county's stance on not competing with the
private sector, particularly in terms of leasing space in the building at market value if it
is leased out in the future.
Commissioner Thompson emphasized the county's proactive approach, noting that
the purchase of the building would help reduce the chance of additional absentee
owners and distressed properties in the downtown core.
Page 6 of 10
```

