Board of County Commissioners
Minutes of the Proceedings - Final
July 2, 2024
Commissioner Holmes discussed the purchase of the building and noted that the
county would not subsidize rental rates. He said the county's building is full, and with
the growing community, there will be a demand for expanded services. He noted that
the county has done its due diligence by hiring consultants to perform inspections and
make the county aware of any potential problems with the building.
Commissioners Holmes and Heath reiterated the county's unwavering commitment to
maintaining offices in the downtown area and ensuring the community's continued
access to essential services.

The motion carried by the following vote:
Lovett, Heath, Holmes, Thompson
Aye:
Malm
