26. PUBLIC HEARING regarding an administrative plat for Tract 1,
Church of Christ Subdivision, 1st Filing, and a zone change from AR -
Agricultural Residential to MU - Mixed Use for Tract 2, Church of
Christ Subdivision, 1st Filing and Tract 2, Church of Christ, 2nd Filing,
Laramie County, WY.
24 - 348
Church of Christ Subdivision, 2nd Filing, Administrative
Plat and Zone Change
Attachments:
Justin Arnold, Planning, said Steil Surveying Services, LLC, on behalf of Cheyenne
Church of Christ and Airport Parkway Church of Christ, submitted zone change and
administrative plat applications. He said the administrative plat is for Tract 1, Church
of Christ Subdivision, 1st Filing, situated in a portion of the SE1/4 of Sect 19, T14N,
R65W of the 6th PM, Laramie County, WY. Arnold said the subject property lies at
4707 Allan Rd, and the 17.19-acre parcel will be divided into two tracts, to be known
as Church of Christ Subdivision, 2nd Filing. He said Tract 1 will be an 11.92-acre
tract, including the existing church, and Tract 2 will have 5.25 acres of vacant land to
sell. Arnold said the zone change for Tract 2, Church of Christ Subdivision, 1st Filing,
and Tract 2, Church of Christ Subdivision, 2nd Filing is to change the zone district
from AR - Agricultural Residential to a MU - Mixed Use zone district to accommodate
commercial uses on the two tracts.
Arnold said based on evidence provided, staff recommends approval of the
administrative plat and zone change with the adoption of findings of fact a, b and c.
Chairman Lovett opened the hearing for PUBLIC COMMENT. James Schick, Clint
Taylor and Bill Eckrich, residents, expressed concerns about the zone change.
Comments were about maintaining a rural lifestyle and a residential neighborhood,
and the lack of information on commercial uses.
Commissioner Thompson spoke about a condition for any site plans to come back to
the board to give residents the ability to make comments on any uses for the property.
Hearing no further PUBLIC COMMENT, Chairman Lovett closed the hearing.
A motion was made by Vice Chairman Malm, seconded by Commissioner
Page 8 of 10
